  "behavior": [
    "Persist user/product/instrument/clientTriggerOrderId before the sole independent placement POST; persist original triggerOrderId before cancellation. Initial storage failure sends nothing.",
    "Unknown/lost/malformed replies retain original intent. Reconstructed AppState/browser reload GET the original committed result; no implicit POST retry or new identity.",
    "A client multi-tier submission stops at the first unknown tier. Already acknowledged and issued-unknown tiers leave the open form; unsent tiers remain. After restart, only the issued request identity is restored; this does not claim durable restoration of unsubmitted form drafts.",
    "Confirmation-storage failure retains the original intent. User/session fences prevent sending remaining old-account tiers and showing old-account results.",
    "Trade-page trigger cancellation and order-page cancellation are disabled for an existing pending request. Both views pass canonical instrument identity; the result button identifies trigger cancellation.",
    "Normal trigger/cancel acknowledgments validate original ID/instrument/owner/status. Native TriggerOrderModel now retains the private owner field for that validation."
  ],
  "backend": {
    "placementRead": "GET /api/v1/gateway/trading-trigger/submission?userId=...&clientTriggerOrderId=...",
    "cancellationRead": "GET /api/v1/gateway/trading-trigger/cancellations/{triggerOrderId}?userId=...",
    "flow": "TradingLocalRoutes → TriggerOrderRequestService → original stable identity → OrderService.commandResult → realtime committed receipt projection",
    "identity": "Placement lookup shares normalized product/user/client identity with prepareTriggerOrder. Cancellation key remains UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes(TRIGGER_CANCEL:user:id), unchanged for existing commands. Lookup validation rejects nonpositive user/ID and blank/overlong client identity.",
    "isolation": "Authenticated user binding; cross-user query parameters rejected. Six-product identity/receipt unit coverage; no online Core query/fallback, new SQL, new protocol or financial-model change.",
    "release": "Deploy matching gateway and both clients; retain existing committed-receipt migration/export and required history repair. No new migration this round.",
    "newAbstractions": "No new production class/interface or framework. Added pure original-key methods and read routes in existing owners; client intent fields reuse the existing settings persistence, read-confirmation UI and private state."
  },
